WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.576
Good morning, John, it's Tuesday- some day of some month.

00:00:02.576 --> 00:00:05.836
I have something I need to get off my chest. There's always been ice on Mars! Everybody knows that there's ice on Mars!

00:00:05.836 --> 00:00:07.579
It's just not news that there's ice on Mars!

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:08.780
Why is that news?

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:12.196
We've known for, like, 50 years that there's ice on Mars!

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:13.420
[sighs deeply] Okay.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:20.540
[intro music]

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:22.500
Sorry.

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:24.400
Mars dork.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:26.700
Mars has ice caps.

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:31.260
They're sometimes coated with carbon dioxide- like, dry ice- but at the core they're both made of water.

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:34.760
I don't why everyone thought that it was news that there's ice on Mars.

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:37.340
The news is that the lander landed on ice.

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:40.880
That's great news for the people who wanted to study the ice, but there- there's always been ice on Mars!

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:47.400
Anyway...couple weeks ago, I asked the Nerdfighters to use their collective brain cells and Googling-fingers to answer some question.

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:49.020
Wee-yoo.

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:52.300
And they did a remarkably good job at all but one of the questions.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:54.780
And the one question that didn't get answered was pretty hard.

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:58.020
I asked what the difference between "mono" and "uni" were, and you guys knew that.

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:01.600
Apparently the big difference is that one is Latin and one is Greek, and I though they were both Latin.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:05.200
Latin words use "uni" and Greek words use "mono."

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:09.880
Now, there were other people who indicated that "uni" often had a connotation of bringing many into one,

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:12.560
whereas "mono" was just one on its own.

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:16.760
Like, monomer is one thing all by itself, whereas university is many coming into one.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:20.513
But does't work in every circumstance, like: unicycles only have one wheel.

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:21.674
It is not a mono-cycle.

00:01:21.674 --> 00:01:22.785
But interesting nonetheless!

00:01:22.785 --> 00:01:24.405
If, uh, you're interested in that kind of thing.

00:01:24.405 --> 00:01:27.464
Continuing: trivia...uh, come from tri-via. I was right.

00:01:27.464 --> 00:01:32.224
Tri-via. Three roads. And any place where three roads come together is often where people would get together and talk about...

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:33.220
They just gossip.

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:36.860
You know, chill out, hang out, talk about stuff that doesn't really matter.

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:38.940
Not very important stuff, but you know...trivia.

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:41.480
"Are there more murders on T.V. or in real life?"

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:42.740
Now that remains pretty much unanswered.

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:48.240
The general consensus is that real life probably has more murders, which, you know, is not what I would want to hear.

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:51.014
Per capita, television definitely has more murders.

00:01:51.014 --> 00:01:54.814
If you're a character on television, your lifespan is significantly shorter than a person in real life.

00:01:54.840 --> 00:02:02.700
Also, if you're at a party and Tony Shalhoub, or Angela Lansbury, or Hercule Poirot show up, just leave.

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:08.460
Leave... Leave.... Run away because I think your jewels are going to get stolen or you are going to get whacked!

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:10.400
I also ask whether evil people have pets.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:12.216
Lots of evil people have had pets.

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:13.380
So lots of people knew about Hitler.

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:18.540
He had a dog named Blondi- a German Shepard (surprise)- that apparently went down the same way as he and his girlfriend:

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:20.060
through poison pill.

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:22.035
But, what you may not know is that Hitler had another dog...

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:23.560
named Fuchsl.

00:02:23.891 --> 00:02:24.851
I'm not making it up.

00:02:24.851 --> 00:02:31.171
So while Hitler was fighting in World War I, he was- he was, uh, working around the trenches and he found a little Terrier named Fuchsl, and he adopted it.

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:33.400
And later, Fuchsl was stolen from him.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:36.872
Whoever stole Fuchsl may in fact have been responsible for Hitler turning out the way he did.

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:37.620
Probably not.

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:40.821
Nonetheless, it's hard to think that if you had a little Terrier named Fuchsl that you could be that much of a jerk.

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:41.900
Fuchsl.

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:42.620
[cute noises]

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:45.000
Lenin loved cats. He had lots of cats.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:50.900
And while you may not think that Lenin is very evil, he did sort of open up the door for Stalin to take over after he died, which...not good.

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:53.800
However, there was some evil people that really, uh, hated pets.

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:56.760
For example, Mao, who you might not think is all that evil until I tell you this story.

00:02:56.760 --> 00:03:02.380
He decided that all pets were a symbol of- of, bourgeoisie oppression and had them all killed, uh, in the sixties and seventies.

00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:05.220
He killed tens of thousands of dogs and cats.

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:07.380
Even dogs and cats that were raised primarily for food.

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:08.480
Uh, he killed those as well.

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:09.840
Not that they would not have died.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:11.620
So now you know the answers to all those questions!

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:12.720
I have a question for you.

00:03:12.740 --> 00:03:16.980
I'm making a song about Star Trek, and it's longer than four minutes, and I can't get it any shorter.

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:24.300
So I'm going to have to impose the one longer-than-four-minutes clause, and that requires that there be a Nerdfighting montage.

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:26.460
So you can send me anything to do with Star Trek. Anything.

00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:30.616
Preferably Next Generation, and preferably with Captain Picard involved.

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:31.940
[quiet grunt] That would be fantastic.

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:34.960
To sparksflyup@gmail.com so that the video can be longer than four minutes.

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:36.060
I promise it'll be worth it.

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:37.320
I'm very excited about the song.

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:38.520
John, I'll see ya soon.

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:44.920
Lenin's kitty says, "Click the little yellow box and subscribe!"

